PREVIOUSLY ON DARK SQUARES

MONTAGE — Keith's freestyle in the backyard. Lucky's final record. Chucky confronting Keith in the rain. The fight. The slam. The silence. Uncle Candyman calling 911. The crooked birthday banner. Manny looking at his brother. The scratch of the needle on the record.

===

TEASER

FADE IN:

EXT. ELLA MAE'S HOUSE, ROCKS — NIGHT — CONTINUOUS

Rain needles the crooked birthday banner. KEITH kneels beside the unresponsive CHUCKY. SARAH presses her coat beneath Chucky's head. UNCLE CANDYMAN stands over both of them, phone to his ear, voice steady.

UNCLE CANDYMAN
Nobody runs. Nobody touches him. The truth is what it is.

Keith's hands won't stop shaking.

KEITH
Chuck...

No answer.

KEITH
I didn't mean to. Manny. Manny, I didn't mean to.

MANNY pushes through the remaining guests to reach his brother. He drops to a knee beside Chucky. He looks, assesses, cannot fix.

MANNY (V.O.)
There is a specific silence that comes after a thing that cannot be undone. The rain was loud. The record was still scratching. But none of that was what I was hearing.

Sirens in the distance. Getting closer.

MANNY (V.O.)
What I was hearing was everything that came before it, every choice, every warning, every moment I thought I was keeping him safe.

TITLE CARD: DARK SQUARES

===

ACT ONE

INT. ELLA MAE'S HOUSE — PRE-DAWN

Police and emergency responders move through the living room and into the yard. The Sweet Sixteen is no longer a party. It is a scene.

The teenagers are separated. Notebooks and questions. The room that an hour ago held music and food and Manny's birthday now holds blue light through the windows.

LUCKY moves quietly through the studio area. He removes the alcohol that Nate brought. He removes his own protection — the gun kept to guard the equipment — and takes it somewhere the responding officers will not find it. He does this without panic. He has thought about this kind of night before.

MANNY stands at the window, watching the ambulance take Chucky away.

MANNY (V.O.)
I watched them load Chucky up and I tried to remember everything I knew about him. Tried to find some version of this night that made sense. Couldn't.

===

EXT. ELLA MAE'S HOUSE — FRONT WALK — PRE-DAWN

BUTCH is moving guests toward the street, toward cabs, toward safe rides home. His phone buzzes — a name he recognizes, someone who wants to know if there is neighborhood business to conduct.

Butch declines the call.

NUTTY NATE and CHEERIO stand at the edge of the walk. Uncle Candyman finds them and moves them out of the immediate scene.

Nate does not delete the Check Check thread. He holds the phone, thinks about it, and does not delete it.

===

INT. HOSPITAL WAITING AREA — MORNING

CHUCKY'S MOTHER sits at one end. She will not meet anyone's eyes.

A DOCTOR appears.

DOCTOR
He is alive. He is critical. The next hours matter.

Sarah closes her eyes.

SARAH
Alive is not the same as all right.

Manny and Keith sit side by side. Keith has not spoken in an hour. His hands are still in his lap.

A DETECTIVE approaches. Asks Keith to come with him for a statement.

===

INT. HOSPITAL — INTERVIEW ROOM — MORNING

KEITH
He swung first. I — we were outside. He swung and I grabbed him and I — I just lifted him. I didn't think about where he was going to land.

DETECTIVE
Have you ever been in a physical altercation before?

KEITH
No.

DETECTIVE
With Chucky?

KEITH
No. He's my friend.

(beat)

He was my friend.

DETECTIVE
The case remains open.

===

EXT. HOSPITAL — MORNING

SARAH
You good?

BUTCH
Doing what needs doing.

His phone buzzes. He declines again.

BUTCH
People will write their own version of tonight if we let them.

MANNY
(stepping out)
We don't get to write it.

===

ACT TWO

INT. ELLA MAE'S KITCHEN — DAY

Ella Mae moves through the kitchen, making calls. Manny is on the front step, on his knees, scrubbing.

UNCLE CANDYMAN
(from doorway)
Leave that.

MANNY
No.

UNCLE CANDYMAN
Being the older brother does not make you the father. You understand me?

MANNY
I should have seen it coming.

UNCLE CANDYMAN
And if you had?

Manny does not answer. That is the answer.

===

INT. ELLA MAE'S KITCHEN — LATER

Ella Mae puts food in front of Keith.

KEITH
I'm not hungry.

ELLA MAE
I did not ask. Eat.

He eats. Mechanically.

ELLA MAE
You're going to tell me exactly what happened. Not tonight. When you're ready. And you're going to tell me the truth.

KEITH
I know.

ELLA MAE
I'm not going to lose you to this.

KEITH
Mom —

ELLA MAE
I said I'm not going to lose you to this. Do you hear me?

KEITH
I hear you.

===

INT. HIGH SCHOOL HALLWAY — FOLLOWING DAY

Sarah moves through the hall.

CLASSMATE
How's Chucky?

SARAH
I don't know.

CLASSMATE
Someone said he's —

SARAH
I don't know.

She does not stop walking.

===

INT. LUCKY'S STUDIO — NIGHT

Lucky lets Keith in. He does not hand him a microphone.

He gives Keith a task: moving equipment, labeling cassettes. Practical work.

LUCKY
A beat can hold a feeling. It can't excuse one.

Later, Lucky hits record before Keith realizes it. Keith is talking — not performing, talking. Lucky saves the rough take.

===

EXT. ROCKS CORNER — NIGHT

BOY GEORGE, an older neighborhood figure, finds Butch.

BOY GEORGE
The way you moved people out. Kept it from getting worse.

BUTCH
I did what needed doing.

BOY GEORGE
I got a situation that could use someone with steady hands.

BUTCH
I'm good.

BOY GEORGE
People are already asking who to talk to around here. That name is starting to be yours.

BUTCH
I didn't ask for it.

BOY GEORGE
Most people who have it didn't.

Manny watches from across the street. He sees the conversation. He files it.

===

ACT THREE

INT. ELLA MAE'S HOUSE — NIGHT

Ella Mae finds Manny in the kitchen at midnight.

ELLA MAE
You need to sleep.

MANNY
I know.

ELLA MAE
I need help, Manny. Not to carry all of it. I need help.

She puts her hand on his shoulder.

ELLA MAE
I don't need to lose you to helping.

MANNY
Yes, ma'am.

ELLA MAE
We've had bad nights before.

MANNY
Not like this.

ELLA MAE
No. Not like this. But we are still here. And tomorrow we are still going to be here. You understand?

MANNY
Yes, ma'am.

===

INT. HOSPITAL — CHUCKY'S ROOM — DAY

Keith stands at the door. He does not go all the way in.

KEITH
(low)
Chuck. I'm sorry. Not because anyone told me to say it. Because I mean it. I know that doesn't change anything. I just need you to know.

He waits. Nothing comes. He steps back into the hall. He does not ask to be forgiven.

===

EXT. GARAGE COURT — DAY

Butch on the court. A neighborhood argument about to go somewhere it should not.

Butch steps between the two kids.

BUTCH
We're not doing this.

KID #1
Tell him that.

BUTCH
I'm telling both of you. Walk it off. Come back tomorrow.

Something in his voice — not threat, not performance — settles the air. The kids separate.

Nate, watching from the side of the court, notes who listened and how fast.

NATE
(to himself)
That's a problem.

===

EXT. ROCKS STREET — EARLY EVENING

A DETECTIVE finds Manny walking home.

DETECTIVE
Emmanuel.

Manny stops.

DETECTIVE
Chucky made it through the night. The investigation is still active.

MANNY
I know.

DETECTIVE
We're going to need your brother available. He's not leaving town. You understand?

MANNY
I'll tell him.

The detective walks away. Manny turns toward home.

===

ACT FOUR

INT. ELLA MAE'S HOUSE — LATE NIGHT

Manny comes in. Keith is at the kitchen table. His schoolwork in front of him. Beside it: a cassette. Beside that: a bill Ella Mae has circled twice.

KEITH
He's alive?

MANNY
Yeah. He made it through the night.

KEITH
Am I going to jail?

The question lands in the room like something dropped from a height.

MANNY
I don't know. We don't know yet. You can't leave town.

KEITH
I didn't mean —

MANNY
I know.

KEITH
I keep saying that.

MANNY
I know you mean it.

Keith puts his face in his hands. Manny sits across from him.

MANNY
We take the next step.

KEITH
Even when it's heavy?

MANNY
Especially then.

===

INT. ELLA MAE'S HOUSE — LATER

Keith finally sleeps at the table. Manny covers him with the throw blanket. Turns off the kitchen light. Sits down in the dark.

ELLA MAE
(from hallway)
Manny.

MANNY
Yeah.

ELLA MAE
Sleep.

He folds his arms on the table and closes his eyes where he sits.

===

TAG

EXT. ROCKS BLOCK — DAWN

The neighborhood wakes around Ella Mae's house. Regular sounds. Cars. Birds. The city going about its business.

Manny comes out to the porch. The birthday banner is still hanging. He looks at it.

He looks at the front step he scrubbed.

He looks at the street, which is just a street again.

He locks the front door. Checks that it is locked. Looks at the repaired porch light.

MANNY (V.O.)
No one is rescued by morning. They are only given another choice.

He can hear the city moving beyond the block. One sound underneath all of it: the scratch of the record.

MANNY (V.O.)
Bloody Sweet 16 was the name the neighborhood was going to give it.

(beat)

We would spend a long time learning what the name meant.

FADE OUT.

END OF EPISODE

